; MAKECOM.HLP - what F1 and HELP show ("help" part) and the end of LIST ("list" part).
help Say what the program should do, a sentence at a time:
help   make screen flash, play sound
help   count down from 10 and beep each time then say liftoff
help   build an alarm clock
help A colon opens a block; the next sentences go inside it:
help   repeat 3 times:      count from 1 to 5:      forever:
help   if it is bigger than 5:      if the key is q:      else
help The blue line is where new code goes.  Up and Down move it, into and
help out of blocks; Tab and Shift-Tab jump from block to block; Home and End
help go to the top and bottom.  Del on an empty line deletes the line below.
help Typed commands: END leaves a block, NEW empties the program, NAME file
help names it, LIST shows the language, QUIT ends.
help F2, or Enter on an empty line, takes up the line below for changing.
help In what you type: Left, Right, Home, End, Del, Ctrl-Left, Ctrl-Right.
help F5 (RUN in a script) runs the program and comes back.  MEM, XMS ON/OFF.
help The program is also kept as text in NAME.SRC; LOAD name takes one up.
help In a script: UP DOWN TOP BOTTOM TAB BACK GO n DEL n EDIT n text SHOW.
help "make an adventure" (or ASK) asks you questions and builds from the answers.
help ASK WORLD builds a room-and-inventory game. WORLD file reads its answers.
list OUT n   ECHO text   LET v=n   INPUT v   STOP
list FOR v=n TO n ... NEXT   FOR v=n DOWNTO n ... NEXT
list TIMES n ... END   FOREVER ... END   IF n<n ... ELSE ... END   REPEAT n
